     pprroooott can fill up a chroot directory for ports building usage.  It will
     perform a set of aaccttiioonnss that should fill up a destination _c_h_r_o_o_t direc‐
     tory from the base system (or an optional _s_r_c_r_o_o_t).

     As far as possible, pprroooott will create hardlinks instead of copying files,
     so that cloning an existing chroot will often only consume i-nodes.

     Some attributes can take multiple values.  As a shorthand, several values
     can be specified in a row without having to repeat the _a_t_t_r_i_b_u_t_e name,
     for instance:

           proot -B /build actions=unpopulate_light check_symlinks

